The GUI exposes a global object getgenv().N0BD_UI after it has been successfully initialized.
This object gives you full control over the hub – adding/removing tabs, creating components, reading/writing values, and customizing the interface.

🔧 Core Properties
        Property	Type	Description
        Version	string	Current version of the UI (e.g. "2.5.2").
        Gui	ScreenGui	The root GUI object.
        Main	Frame	The main window frame.
        Sidebar	Frame	The sidebar container (holds tabs).
        Content	Frame	The content area where pages are displayed.
        Theme	table	Color theme used throughout the UI (read‑only). Contains keys like BG, Card, Accent, etc.
        Pages	table	Dictionary of all pages (keyed by tab name). Each entry has Page (ScrollingFrame), Stack (Frame), List (UIListLayout), Refresh (function).
        Tabs	table	Dictionary of all tab buttons (keyed by tab name). Each entry is the TextButton instance.
        Components	table	Registry containing all components, grouped by type (All, Buttons, Toggles, Sliders, Labels, Cards, Headers, Dividers, Dropdowns, Inputs).
        Buttons	table	Alias for Components.Buttons.
        Toggles	table	Alias for Components.Toggles.
        Sliders	table	Alias for Components.Sliders.
        Labels	table	Alias for Components.Labels.
        Cards	table	Alias for Components.Cards.
        Headers	table	Alias for Components.Headers.
        Dividers	table	Alias for Components.Dividers.
        Dropdowns	table	Alias for Components.Dropdowns.
        Inputs	table	Alias for Components.Inputs.
        ToggleKey	Enum.KeyCode	Current hotkey for showing/hiding the hub (default: Enum.KeyCode.RightShift).
        AntiAfkInterval	number	Interval (in seconds) between anti‑AFK jump pulses (default: 300).

🛠 Methods – General
        Toast(message: string)
        Shows a temporary toast notification at the bottom‑right corner.
        Example: N0BD_UI.Toast("Hello world!")

        SelectTab(tabName: string)
        Switches to the given tab (must already exist).
        Example: N0BD_UI.SelectTab("Main")

        AddTab(name: string, icon?: string) -> PageObject
        Creates a new tab with the given name and optional icon (e.g. "⚙").
        Returns the page object ({ Page, Stack, List, Refresh }).
        Example: local page = N0BD_UI.AddTab("Settings", "⚙")

        RemoveTab(name: string)
        Removes a tab (cannot remove the "Main" tab).
        Example: N0BD_UI.RemoveTab("Settings")

        SetToggleKey(key: Enum.KeyCode)
        Changes the hotkey used to toggle the hub visibility.
        Example: N0BD_UI.SetToggleKey(Enum.KeyCode.F1)

🔍 Component Lookup
        All Get... functions return the component object (if found) or nil. They accept a component ID (string) that was specified when the component was created (or auto‑generated from its title).

        Function	Returns
        Get(id)	Any component by ID.
        GetButton(id)	Button component (action card).
        GetToggle(id) / GetSwitch(id)	Toggle component.
        GetSlider(id)	Slider component.
        GetLabel(id)	Label component.
        GetCard(id)	Card frame.
        GetHeader(id)	Header label.
        GetDivider(id)	Divider frame.
        GetTab(id)	Tab button.
        GetPage(id)	Page object.
        GetDropdown(id)	Dropdown component.
        GetInput(id)	Text‑input component.
        Example:

        --lua
        local toggle = N0BD_UI.GetToggle("AntiAFK")
        if toggle then toggle.Enable() end

📋 Listing Components
        Function	Returns
        ListAll()	Full component registry (Components.All).
        ListButtons()	Dictionary of all button components.
        ListToggles()	Dictionary of all toggle components.
        ListSliders()	Dictionary of all slider components.
        ListLabels()	Dictionary of all label components.
        ListCards()	Dictionary of all card frames.
        ListDropdowns()	Dictionary of all dropdown components.
        ListInputs()	Dictionary of all text‑input components.
        ListComponents(kind?: string)	If kind is given (e.g. "Buttons"), returns that sub‑registry; otherwise returns Components.All.

🧩 Component Registration (Advanced)
        RegisterComponent(kind, id, object, aliases?)
        Registers a custom component under a given kind and ID.
        Used internally, but can be used to add your own entries.

        UnregisterComponent(kind, id)
        Removes a component from the registry.

🏗 Component Builders
        All builder functions create a new component inside a given page and return the component object.
        They accept an optional options table (or a string as ID) that can contain:

        Id – custom identifier (string)

        Aliases – table of additional IDs to register

        Component‑specific options (e.g. ButtonWidth)

        AddHeader(page, text, options?) -> HeaderLabel
        Adds a section header.
        Example: N0BD_UI.AddHeader(myPage, "General Settings", "GeneralHeader")

        AddDivider(page, options?) -> DividerFrame
        Adds a horizontal separator line.

        AddCard(page, name?, options?) -> CardFrame
        Adds a blank card container (with automatic height).
        Useful for grouping custom content.

        AddActionCard(page, title, description, buttonText, options?) -> (card, button)
        Creates a card with a title, description, and a button.
        Returns both the card frame and the button component object.
        Example:

        --lua
            local card, btn = N0BD_UI.AddActionCard(page, "Rejoin", "Rejoin the server", "REJOIN", "RejoinBtn")
            btn.Click(function()
                -- action
             end)

        AddToggle(page, title, description, defaultValue, callback?, options?) -> ToggleObject
        Creates an ON/OFF toggle.
        callback is called with the new state (boolean) whenever the toggle changes.
        ToggleObject methods:

        Get() / IsEnabled() → current state

        Set(bool), Enable(), Disable(), Toggle()

        SetSilent(bool) – changes state without calling the callback

        Button – the actual TextButton

        Card, Title, Description

        AddSlider(page, title, description, min, max, default, callback?, options?) -> SliderObject
        Creates a slider with a numeric value.
        callback receives the new integer value.
        SliderObject methods:

        Get() → current value

        Set(value) – clamps to min/max

        GetMin(), GetMax()

        Card, Bar, Fill, Knob, Title, ValueLabel, Description

        AddLabel(page, title, valueText?, options?) -> LabelObject
        Displays a key‑value pair.
        Methods: SetValue(v), GetValue(), SetTitle(v), GetTitle(), SetColor(c)
        Properties: Title, Value, Card.

        AddDropdown(page, title, optionsTable, default?, callback?, options?) -> DropdownObject
        Creates a dropdown selector.
        optionsTable is an array of strings/numbers.
        callback is called with the selected value.
        DropdownObject methods:

        Get() → current selected value

        GetIndex() → index of selected option

        Set(value) – selects by value

        SetIndex(idx) – selects by index

        Options – the option array

        Card, Button, Title

        AddTextInput(page, title, placeholder, buttonText?, callback?, options?) -> InputObject
        Creates a text field with a submit button.
        The input is submitted either by clicking the button or pressing Enter while the field is focused.
        callback is called with the entered text (if empty, the placeholder is used).
        InputObject methods:

        Get() → current saved text

        Set(value) – updates the field and calls the callback

        Button, TextBox, Card, Title

        All Add... functions have an equivalent Create... alias (e.g. CreateToggle, CreateSlider, etc.) for consistency.

📦 Component Object Common Properties
        Every component object returned by the builders (or retrieved via Get...) includes at least:

        Id – the component’s unique ID

        Type – the kind (e.g. "Buttons", "Toggles")

        Card – the frame that contains the component (if applicable)

        IsVisible() → boolean

        SetVisible(bool) – shows/hides the component’s card

🔄 Example Workflow
        --lua
            local UI = getgenv().N0BD_UI
            if not UI then return end

        -- Add a new tab
        local myPage = UI.AddTab("MyTab", "📁")

        -- Add a header
        UI.AddHeader(myPage, "My Controls")

        -- Add a toggle
        local myToggle = UI.AddToggle(myPage, "Enable Feature", "Turns the feature on/off", false, function(state)
            print("Feature is now", state)
        end, "FeatureToggle")

        -- Add a slider
        UI.AddSlider(myPage, "Speed", "Set the speed", 1, 100, 50, function(val)
            print("Speed set to", val)
        end, "SpeedSlider")

        -- Add a dropdown
        UI.AddDropdown(myPage, "Mode", {"Easy", "Medium", "Hard"}, "Medium", function(val)
            print("Mode:", val)
        end, "ModeDropdown")

        -- Add a text input
        UI.AddTextInput(myPage, "Chat Message", "Enter your message", "Send", function(msg)
            print("Sending:", msg)
        end, "ChatInput")

        -- Later, retrieve and manipulate
        local toggle = UI.GetToggle("FeatureToggle")
        toggle.Enable()
        local speed = UI.GetSlider("SpeedSlider")
        speed.Set(75)

🧹 Cleanup
        The GUI also provides a cleanup function:

        lua
        getgenv().N0BD_Cleanup()
        This destroys the GUI, disconnects all events, and clears the global references.

📝 Notes
        All IDs are automatically sanitized (non‑alphanumeric characters removed). If you provide an ID, make sure it is unique.

        The options parameter in builders can be a string (which becomes the ID) or a table with fields like Id, Aliases, ButtonWidth, etc.

        The callback functions are executed inside a task.spawn, so they are safe to yield.
